# Configuration template for docker-compose.logtriage.yaml (log triage, Phase C)
#
# Copy to .env.logtriage (cp env.logtriage.example .env.logtriage) and fill in.
# The file is gitignored and is passed to compose with --env-file by the
# logtriage make targets.
#
# Nothing secret belongs here. The stack's generated credentials live in
# .secrets/logtriage/stack.env, written by `make logtriage-secrets`, and the
# make targets pass both files. Keeping them apart means this one stays
# hand-editable and diffable without a password in it.
#
# The three LOGTRIAGE_*_URL/URI variables are read by the tool rather than by
# compose, and they are the whole of its configuration: the same code runs
# against these services on the workstation and against a native llama-server
# on the MacBook, with no code path selected by hostname.

# --- Read by compose, to start the services ---------------------------------

# GGUF served for triage. Must be a tool-calling-capable instruction-tuned
# model; the loop is useless without native tool calls.
LOGTRIAGE_LLM_MODEL=/app/models/gguf/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF/gemma-4-31B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf

# GGUF served for embeddings. A dedicated embedding model, not the chat model:
# llama.cpp's embedding mode replaces the chat endpoints, so this is a separate
# server, and a 31B model producing embeddings would cost VRAM the triage model
# needs for no retrieval benefit.
LOGTRIAGE_EMBED_MODEL=/app/models/gguf/nomic-embed-text-v1.5-GGUF/nomic-embed-text-v1.5.Q8_0.gguf

# Context sizes. The triage context holds a whole log profile plus retrieved
# documentation; the embedding context only needs to exceed the chunker's
# MAX_TOKENS, and anything larger is VRAM taken from the model beside it.
# LOGTRIAGE_LLM_CTX=32768
# LOGTRIAGE_EMBED_CTX=8192

# Pooling strategy for the embedding server (mean|cls|last). Must match what
# the model was trained with, or the vectors are well-formed and meaningless.
# LOGTRIAGE_EMBED_POOLING=mean

# llama.cpp's parsing of the model's reasoning channel. Left empty until it is
# measured whether Gemma's thinking leaks into content against the official
# chat template; see logtriage/docs/verification/desktop.md.
# LOGTRIAGE_REASONING_FORMAT=

# --- Read by the tool, to reach the services --------------------------------

# Omit any of these and the tool uses its offline implementation instead, which
# is how the whole pipeline runs in a checkout with nothing installed.

# LOGTRIAGE_MONGO_URI=mongodb://logtriage:<password>@127.0.0.1:27017/?authSource=admin&replicaSet=rs0&directConnection=true
# LOGTRIAGE_LLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8006
# LOGTRIAGE_EMBED_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8007

# Where `logtriage fetch-kb` clones the MongoDB manual from. Point it at a
# local path or a mirror to provision a machine without re-cloning from GitHub.
# LOGTRIAGE_KB_SOURCE=
